@@ -162,17 +162,21 @@ the source code only. This has several implications:
   A future version of mwparserfromhell may include multiple parsing modes to
   get around this restriction more sensibly.
 
-Additionally, the parser lacks awareness of certain wiki-specific settings:
+Additionally, the parser knows nothing about the wiki the text comes from
+unless it is told. Passing a ``mwparserfromhell.SiteInfo`` profile as the
+*site* argument of ``mwparserfromhell.parse()`` fills these gaps; without one:
 
-* `Word-ending links`_ are not supported, since the linktrail rules are
-  language-specific.
+* `Word-ending links`_ are not attached to the link, since the linktrail rules
+  are language-specific. ``SiteInfo(linktrail=...)`` names the characters that
+  may form a trail, which the parser then stores in ``Wikilink.trail``.
 
 * Localized namespace names aren't recognized, so file links (such as
-  ``[[File:...]]``) are treated as regular wikilinks.
+  ``[[File:...]]``) are treated as regular wikilinks. ``SiteInfo(namespaces=...)``
+  maps namespace names and aliases to their ids and fills ``Wikilink.namespace``.
 
 * Anything that looks like an XML tag is treated as a tag, even if it is not a
   recognized tag name, since the list of valid tags depends on loaded MediaWiki
-  extensions.
+  extensions. ``SiteInfo(tags=...)`` restricts tag parsing to the listed names.
 
 Integration
 -----------
